From 3848d051f8dc65371b40b992c8511dfd62db2bf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:43:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: en751221: xr500v: initialize the environment on first
 boot

The migration helper creates empty ubootenv and ubootenv2 volumes.
Until U-Boot saves its board environment, Linux fw_env has no valid
copy. A Linux fw_setenv using its generic fallback defaults can then
persist a bootcmd that is not the XR500v boot path.

Add a first-boot marker to the default environment and check it from
the default bootcmd. Remove the marker before exporting the environment
and call saveenv twice. On the successful path, env_ubi_save writes the
primary volume from ENV_INVALID, changes env_valid to ENV_VALID, then
writes the redundant volume. Both saved copies omit the marker.

Existing saved environments without this marker do not need rewriting.
Keep booting if saving fails; this is not a transactional repair scheme
and a failed save can leave fewer than two valid copies.

The same code was exercised in the daily integration with existing
valid environments. The recent hardware run did not exercise saving
into two empty UBI volumes.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 defenvs/en751221_tplink_archer-xr500v-v1 | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/defenvs/en751221_tplink_archer-xr500v-v1 b/defenvs/en751221_tplink_archer-xr500v-v1
index cdd6ac5c..2a091b57 100644
--- a/defenvs/en751221_tplink_archer-xr500v-v1
+++ b/defenvs/en751221_tplink_archer-xr500v-v1
@@ -48,7 +48,13 @@ format_ubi_part=\
     echo "OEM backups missing or invalid: nothing erased"; \
   fi
 
-bootcmd=run boot_ubi
+# format_ubi_part leaves ubootenv/ubootenv2 empty. Save this environment in
+# both of them on the first boot: until then Linux's fw_setenv finds no valid
+# copy and would store its own generic default environment (bootcmd=run
+# distro_bootcmd) instead, and U-Boot would stop booting OpenWrt. _init_env
+# removes itself, so a saved environment never runs it again.
+_init_env=setenv _init_env; saveenv; saveenv
+bootcmd=if env exists _init_env; then run _init_env; fi; run boot_ubi
 bootdelay=1
 bootmenu_confirm_return=askenv - Press ENTER to return to menu ; bootmenu 20
 bootmenu_default=0
